From 8b0562018db242385c16dee89d865e776da8b56c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mkinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 10:45:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(2d): take a picked contour start under control or
 wear compensation

A picked start point on a closed 2D Contour was refused for control and
wear compensation. The ring now starts at the pick's projection, and a
new check (contour_comp_pick::picked_seam) proves the compensation seam
law there: the first and last cuts are straight and on one line through
the seam, and under control the part contour runs straight there too.
A pick on a corner arc or a vertex is refused by name, never moved.

Item 4 of #1473. Items 5 to 7 stay open.

Refs #1473

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
